 "method": "R19 #42: design search for a buildable gripper mount (new file; reads only, writes results/r19/mount/design*.json).\n\nFor each arm (ur5e_enc2_pgc: the k-DOP wrist-3 hulls; fr5_j6_pgc: the FR5 wrist-3 cylinder) the wrist-3 collision geoms\nare taken from the built scene into the UR flange convention (r19mount.py: F, u = +x_F, the side the gripper base sits on;\nthe FR5 geoms are turned back by its clock_deg). A candidate mount (r19mount.MOUNTS format) moves the housing pieces\n(R_gripper_oem_*, R_gripper_palm, as built) rigidly and adds the bracket pieces. Gate: every housing piece and the bracket\nbody >= 5 mm from every wrist-3 geom (the gripper / held gate); the mating boss is reported, exempt (bolted mating face).\nDistances: mj_geomDistance (signed, distmax 0.2 m) in a small model holding only these geoms, and distance.Bounds.pair (the\nchecker's GJK lower bound, >= 0) as a cross-check.\nSearches (TCP change = the rigid motion applied to the current TCP; rotation = rot_deg):\n C1  same tilt and offset, move along the flange axis only: smallest dz that passes on both arms;\n C4  same tilt, move along the flange axis and radially (du, dz grid, 2.5 mm): smallest |TCP change| that passes;\n C2  wedge: same tilt, face centre (cu, h) on a wedge over the flange; buildability: face low edge >= WALL above the\n     flange face, robot-side M6 counterbores (PCD 50 at +-45 deg) under >= SCREW_H of material; smallest |TCP change|;\n C3  inline: gripper axis on J6 (turned 26.6 deg), DH flange on an ISO 50 spacer of thickness t (0 and 10 mm reported).\npython r19mount_design.py [STEP=.0025] [PART=all|L|hull|wedge|inline|mounts] [FRESH=1] -> results/r19/mount/design[_<PART>].json\n(the wrist-3 / housing geometry is cached in results/r19/mount/geo_cache.pkl; FRESH=1 rebuilds it)",
